# ==============================================================================
# Here we check for obfuscation patterns in subject lines
#
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Language: -
# Weight:   6.0
#           1.0 (use muliplicator 0.17)
#           2.0 (use muliplicator 0.34)
# ==============================================================================

# Obfuscation patterns
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Safer version: only split words with repeated soft-hyphen-like gaps, avoiding the broader
# hidden Unicode separator pattern that can trigger false positives.
/[a-z](?:[­]{1,4})[a-z](?:[­]{1,4})[a-z]/i

# Detect standalone bidirectional control characters used to spoof visual order
# /[‮‬‭‪‫⁦⁧⁨⁩]/i

# Detect text wrapped in RLO/PDF markers (U+202E ... U+202C), a common masking trick
# /‮.{0,80}‬/i

# Detect repeated invisible Unicode separator characters used as letter gaps or placeholders
# /[​‌‍﻿‏⁠]{4,}/i

#
#
#

# Example: "Ak­tu­ali­sie­rung" goes to "Ak-tu-ali-sie-rung" (with a soft hyphen in the middle)
/(=c2=ad|\x\{00ad\})/i

